### Edge Middleware

#### [MODIFY] [middleware.ts](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/FocusForge/CODEKADA/middleware.ts)
- Refreshes Supabase session tokens on every request (required by `@supabase/ssr`).
- Route protection logic:
  - `/login`, `/signup` → redirect to dashboard if already authenticated.
  - `/(student)/*` → require auth + `STUDENT` role.
  - `/(teacher)/*` → require auth + `TEACHER` or `ADMIN` role.
- Role is read from the Prisma `User` table via a lightweight lookup (cached in cookie/session metadata to avoid repeated DB calls).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Middleware runs at the Edge. We cannot use Prisma directly in Edge middleware. Instead, the role will be stored as user metadata in Supabase Auth (`app_metadata.role`) during signup, and read from the JWT in middleware. The Prisma `User.role` remains the source of truth and is synced on login.

